WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.8 · Financial Management
Financial reporting: board, funders and statutory

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know every financial report you will owe, and make every figure come from the same accounts.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Financial reporting means giving each audience the financial information it needs, in its format and by its deadline. Founders, funders, regulators and investors need different reports, all drawn from the same accounts.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Who needs what

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.241
Founders, later a board: Regular management accounts, the cash position and the main financial risks. For example: Two co-founders review a one-page report on the first Monday of each month.

6
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:48.089
Funders: Reports in their own format, showing how their money was used. For example: A six-month grant report showing pilot spending against the agreed budget.

7
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:58.678
Regulators and tax: Statutory accounts and returns by fixed deadlines, once you are registered. For example: The cooperative’s annual accounts and tax return, due on dates set by law.

8
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:09.356
Members and investors: Their own reports, as your legal form or your agreements require. For example: Cooperative members receive the annual accounts before the general meeting.

9
00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:10.356
Why reporting builds trust

10
00:01:10.356 --> 00:01:16.030
1. Missing a statutory deadline can bring fines or harm your registration.

11
00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:21.333
2. The same numbers everywhere build trust with funders and partners.

12
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:28.007
3. Evidence filed from day one makes every report faster to prove.

13
00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:29.007
What you will build

14
00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:35.422
1. A reporting calendar: each deadline, its owner and where the figures come from.

15
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:41.096
2. A filing system: receipts, timesheets and contracts by fund and period.

16
00:01:41.096 --> 00:01:48.511
3. A simple public summary, to be open about your money from the start.

17
00:01:48.911 --> 00:01:49.511
What to avoid

18
00:01:49.511 --> 00:01:54.444
Starting the calendar only after a deadline is missed.

19
00:01:54.444 --> 00:01:59.378
Giving funders figures that do not match your accounts.

20
00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:06.052
Leaving the accounts to the accountant without understanding or approving them.

21
00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:08.452
You build your first financial reporting calendar.

22
00:02:08.452 --> 00:02:12.452
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:17.052
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
